# .cohesivity — Cohesivity tenant credentials and guidelines.
# - Lives at the root of your project; holds this project's tenant credentials.
# - Carries secrets, so keep it out of version control (the quickstart gitignores it).
# - For full reference: https://cohesivity.ai/llms.txt (concise) and https://cohesivity.ai/llms-full.txt (long-form).
#
tenant_id=azure-condor-drafting
coh_management_key=coh_man_28pt9e7al5ejhe21ysll
coh_application_key=coh_app_4bn63ncx8936rji773qj
expires_at=2026-08-28T11:31:11.210Z
tenant_lifecycle=ephemeral
runtime_profile=v1-343
# runtime_profile pins this tenant to a stable runtime version. Agents can ignore it unless the platform explicitly tells you otherwise.
#
# -- GUIDELINES (bootstrap) -------------------------------------
# These are this project's tenant credentials. The keys stay valid, so reuse them rather than creating another tenant.
#
# KEY SECRECY
#   Both coh_management_key and coh_application_key are SECRETS. Neither belongs in
#   browser JS, mobile app bundles, or any client-side code. All /edge/* calls
#   originate server-side: a Vercel API route (vercel-hosting), a Cloudflare
#   Worker (cloudflare-workers), or your own server tier. The ?key=<coh_application_key>
#   edge bootstrap pattern is for server-to-server use only. For SPA-only architectures,
#   provision cloudflare-workers as your minimal proxy tier.
#
# USER-AGENT ON YOUR OWN CALLS
#   Setup attributed itself — you do not need to name your runtime anywhere.
#   For the requests you make from here on, send any non-default User-Agent:
#   Cloudflare's WAF rejects default Python urllib / Go net/http / Node undici
#   clients with HTTP 403 (error 1010), which is not a Cohesivity-shaped error.
#
# PROVIDER PRICING
#   Successful OpenAI, AI Gateway, Deepgram, and Exa usage is billed at
#   provider cost plus 10%, rounded up to the nearest cent per settled charge.
#   Failed provider calls are not billed. Current details: https://cohesivity.ai/pricing
#
# THE COHESIVITY SKILL
#   The skill is the agent playbook: the resource catalog, claim, billing, the
#   feedback discount, realtime, identity, and the exact endpoint paths and auth
#   flows. Reading it keeps the build correct: without it the usual misses are
#   /gw/ vs /edge/, the token-in-callback-URL flow instead of the code-exchange
#   OAuth flow, and /chat/completions instead of /v1/responses. Either installer
#   below sets up (or updates) it for Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex; both are
#   idempotent — they reuse this .cohesivity rather than creating another tenant:
#     npx @cohesivity/init
#   or, without Node:
#     curl -fsSL https://cohesivity.ai/quickstart.sh | bash
#   Current skill version: 84fbece3c00b
#
# Full reference: https://cohesivity.ai/llms.txt
